BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Living Archives: An Oral History Workshop Series (Session 1\, virt
 ual) — Providence
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261105T163000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261105T173000
DTSTAMP:20261106T065326Z
UID:37be5ebfb5190e278ec08a8eb5c1@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures\, Seminars and Workshops\,Providence\,
 United States
DESCRIPTION:How do you move from an idea to an interview-ready oral histor
 y project? This hands-on session walks participants through the essential 
 steps of planning an oral history initiative\, including defining goals\, 
 conducting research\, addressing sensitive subject matter\, and preparing 
 ethically. Participants will apply these concepts by collaboratively creat
 ing a mock oral history project plan\, gaining practical tools they can ad
 apt to academic or community settings. No prior experience with archives\,
  oral history\, or historical research is necessary. All three sessions mu
 st be attended to receive an Oral History Certificate.\nCategory: Lectures
 \, Seminars and Workshops\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/libr
 ary/event/livingarchivesvirtualsession1
LOCATION:Zoom\, Zoom
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.brown.edu/library/event/livingarchivesvirtualsession1
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:brown-arts
END:VEVENT
