DESCRIPTION:Camp One Heartland is a solo exhibition by Tye DuSold-O’Conn
 or archiving documentation of one of the world’s first nonprofit summer 
 camps designated to supporting and empowering youth affected by HIV and AI
 DS\, eventually transforming into a vital beacon of safety\, liberation an
 d eutopia for LGBTQ+ youth across the country. After its inaugural session
  in the summer of 1993 and many more held at different campsites across th
 e country\, Camp One Heartland found its permanent residence in Willow Riv
 er\, Minnesota. Over the next three decades it broadened its reach to prov
 ide summer camp sessions for youth experiencing housing instability\, LGBT
 Q+ youth\, and specifically trans youth. Tye attended Ca\nCategory: Arts &
