DESCRIPTION:Presented after extensive research\, this exhibition recontext
 ualizes African material culture objects held in the GW Collection for nea
 rly 50 years. Led by Assistant Professor Clement Akpang\, 59 students from
  four seminar courses offered between Fall 2024 and Spring 2026\, conducte
 d original research to deepen understanding of the university’s holdings
  and update how we interpret and exhibit these objects. The exhibition fea
 tures 37 tangible heritage objects\, ranging from an Egúngún Paaka from 
 Yorubaland to a Kii [brass pipe]\, attributed to the Baumum people of Came
 roon\, accompanied by images and video that illuminate their rich historie
 s. Research on the entire collection is presented in an \nCategory: Arts &
