DESCRIPTION:Join us for a book launch celebrating Professor of English Ale
 xa Alice Joubin's new book\, Transitional Shakespeare\, Gender\, and Adapt
 ion . About the Book The cross-gender role is a staple of Shakespeare’s 
 plays\, and drama is a transitional art. Gender is made flesh and brought 
 into being by actors’ embodiment. Similarly\, adaptations also operate t
 ransitionally. Some adaptations translate narratives into hospitable forms
  of expression. Other adaptations function as minor uses of established ge
 nres and gender categories. In Transitional Shakespeare\, Gender\, and Ada
 ption \, Professor Alexa Alice Joubin\, PhD\, theorizes “transness” in
  a number of modes\, including composite figures in drama that ar\nCategor
 y: Academic\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/book-launch-
 transitional-shakespeare-gender-and-adaption
