 ates
DESCRIPTION:As local journalism declines\, media ownership consolidates\, 
 and Americans increasingly turn to social media and AI tools for political
  information\, the American information landscape is undergoing a profound
  transformation. What do these changes mean for public trust\, political p
 articipation and the health of our democracy? In the wake of the 2026 midt
 erm elections\, the Institute for Data\, Democracy and Politics (IDDP) wil
 l host a keynote by leading independent journalist Aaron Parnas \, and a p
 anel discussion featuring Michelle Cottle of the New York Times \, Letici
 a Bode of Georgetown University\, and Danny Hayes of George Washington Uni
 versity\, moderated by Michael Tomasky of the New Republi\nCategory: Lect
 ures & Speakers\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/the-stat
